---
import UtilityLayout from "../../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
import UtilityApp from "../../components/UtilityApp.astro";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="Find a meeting time"
  description="Find a time that works across time zones. No calendar connection needed."
  slug="meeting-time-finder"
>
  <UtilityApp tool="meeting" />
  <details class="prose tool-help">
    <summary>How this tool works &amp; limits</summary>
    <h2>Find shared time, not just timezone offsets</h2>
    <p>
      Enter each participant’s timezone and available window for a specific
      local date. The tool intersects the windows and respects one optional
      excluded interval per participant. Jev can interpret explicit times in
      short availability statements; review the populated fields before
      computing.
    </p>
    <h2>Supported availability</h2>
    <p>
      Start with “from 9am until 5pm, but not between noon and 1pm.” Include
      explicit start/end times or enter missing boundaries manually. Each
      participant can have one allowed window and one blocked interval.
      Different weekdays, recurring schedules and multiple allowed windows
      require manual resolution; no holidays, live calendars or actual
      attendance are inferred.
    </p>
    <h2>Daylight saving and local dates</h2>
    <p>
      Offsets are calculated for the exact selected date using IANA timezone
      rules, including half-hour and quarter-hour zones. Ambiguous and
      nonexistent local times at clock changes are rejected. An end earlier than
      its start is interpreted as the next day; every participant’s starting
      window uses the selected local date, which can rule out overlap across the
      international date line.
    </p>
    <p>
      Results are proposals. Downloading an event does not book a meeting,
      contact anyone or establish their availability. Calendar files contain a
      generic Meeting title; private availability statements are not included.
    </p>
  </details>
</UtilityLayout>
